        "title": "Riemannian Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A Riemannian metric turns a smooth manifold into a metric space with notions of length, angle, area, and volume. Geodesics generalize straight lines; the exponential map connects linear algebra at a point to the curved geometry globally."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RIEMANNIAN-GEOMETRY.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-RIEMANNIAN-GEOMETRY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:differential-geometry:04-riemannian-geometry, git-history:differential-geometry:04-riemannian-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "differential-geometry/04-RIEMANNIAN-GEOMETRY.md",
        "concepts": "[riemannian, geometry]",
        "current_path": "differential-geometry/04-RIEMANNIAN-GEOMETRY.md",
        "id": "maxim:differential-geometry:riemannian-geometry",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "differential-geometry",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[riemannian, geometry]",
        "section": "differential-geometry",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Riemannian Geometry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  RIEMANNIAN METRIC g                                             |\n|  Smooth inner product assigned to each tangent space.            |\n|  g = g_ij dx^i tensor dx^j   (in coordinates)                    |\n|                                                                  |\n|       |                                                          |\n|       v                                                          |\n|  LENGTH of curves, ANGLES between vectors, VOLUME of regions     |\n|       |                                                          |\n|       v                                                          |\n|  GEODESICS (locally length-minimizing curves)                    |\n|  Solve: gamma'' + Gamma^k_ij gamma'^i gamma'^j = 0               |\n|       |                                                          |\n|       v                                                          |\n|  EXPONENTIAL MAP: exp_p: T_p M -> M                              |\n|  RIEMANNIAN DISTANCE: d(p,q) = inf_curves L                      |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
